PASS run of the #169 regression file, on merged main (28db2f5).

The same file, unchanged, that counterfactual.log records failing six of nine
when the three isCurrent(...) guards are removed. Criterion-by-criterion:

  criterion 1 + 2  "criterion 1+2: neither token is re-persisted, through the
                    real repository refresh and the real logout"
  criterion 1      "criterion 1: a refresh that resolves inside its own session
                    still persists both tokens"  (the guard does not break the
                    path it guards)
  criterion 3      "criterion 3: queued requests are rejected, not replayed,
                    when the session ended during the refresh"
  criterion 4      "criterion 4: the retryCount == 1 forced logout survives a
                    refresh already in flight"
  criterion 5      "criterion 5: the interceptor refreshes normally again after
                    a subsequent login"

Plus three tests that are not criteria but are what make the fix trustworthy:

  - "the guard does not lean on the cached user blob ..." - #85's second check
    is no longer load-bearing.
  - "a login completing during an old refresh keeps the new session ..." - the
    new session's tokens are neither overwritten nor cleared.
  - "the real provider graph shares one SessionGeneration ..." - two instances
    would pass every other test here and still ship the bug.

